\begin{abstract}
We introduce UV-SIM v4.2-AEROSPACE, a unified relativistic--quantum simulation 
framework designed to model coupled Kerr spacetime dynamics, quantum superfluid 
turbulence, and topological vortex invariants at large-scale adaptive mesh 
resolutions. The relativistic sector employs fourth-order spatial stencils and a 
dimensionally consistent Courant--Friedrichs--Lewy condition to achieve stable 
convergence of the Boyer--Lindquist frame-dragging angular velocity field at 
resolutions up to $16384^3$ nodes. The quantum sector implements a unitary 
split-operator propagator for the time-dependent Gross--Pitaevskii equation, 
preserving the normalization invariant to machine precision across extended 
temporal evolutions. Topological circulation quantization 
$\oint\nabla\phi\cdot d\mathbf{l}=2\pi n$ is maintained exactly under AMR 
refinement, enabling robust tracking of vortex-core dynamics. Laboratory and 
stress-testing benchmarks demonstrate real-time ingestion of multi-messenger 
astrophysical telemetry through a quantum-resistant homomorphic encryption 
pipeline. The combined results establish UV-SIM v4.2-AEROSPACE as a reproducible 
multi-physics platform suitable for high-fidelity studies of relativistic 
frame-dragging, quantum turbulence, and topological vortex structures.
\end{abstract}